Steps:
[NAV] Navigate to Security > Users at {{BACK_URL}}
[ACT] Open existing user
[ACT] Change StoreId field to {{STORE_ID}}
[ACT] Click Save
[WAIT] Wait for save to complete

[NAV] Navigate to Security > Users at {{BACK_URL}}
[ACT] Enter search term 'user_1' in search field
[ASSERT] Verify results

Assertions:
[STATE] Admin SPA shows a clean sign-in screen — no broken/frozen blade left on screen {OBSERVED}
[NETWORK] the triggering API call returns HTTP 401 (not a 302 the SPA's XHR handling cannot follow) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the sign-in page's username and password fields are visible and enabled (not frozen/disabled) {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the category-link action is pre-emptively disabled/blocked client-side with a visible permission-denied message (e.g. "your role does not have permission to link them") and non-interactive selection controls — this is the correct enforcement point for THIS action, not a bug {OBSERVED}
[NETWORK] a reachable forbidden call for this role (e.g. GET /api/platform/modules) returns HTTP 403 directly {OBSERVED}
[STATE] no intermediate 302→AccessDenied→404 redirect chain is observed for that call {OBSERVED}

[NAV] each anonymous navigation to {{BACK_URL}} lands on the sign-in screen via a client-side route (not a raw 401 page) {SPEC}
[STATE] sign-in completes and lands on the Admin SPA home/dashboard on both cycles {OBSERVED}
[NETWORK] no infinite redirect/retry loop on POST /api/platform/security/login/ on either cycle {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] Response status is 200 (health endpoint is intentionally unauthenticated) {SPEC}
[BODY] Response body does not contain a connection string, password, or API key value anywhere in the JSON {SPEC}
[BODY] Per-check Description/Data fields describe status only (e.g. 'Redis responded to PING in 1 ms'), not raw configuration values {OBSERVED}
